<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs rises as Dow stages second biggest rally.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs rises as Dow stages second biggest rally.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs rose as the Dow made one its second biggest one-day gain, up 179 points, 2.64 percent, to 6962.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	  Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28 1/8	 nil</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$29 1/8	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$21 3/8	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13 1/2	 +0 3/8</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$36 1/4	 +0 1/2</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$17 7/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  167 p	     nil</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  39		  +0 1/2</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  234		 nil</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  152 3/4	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Templeton	London  145		 +0 3/4</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.05	    +0.02</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.67	    +0.01</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.22	    -0.01</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of eight shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
